bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:522:* The Handle surface adapters: four surfaces stand as type and vocabulary; loopback first, then DNS control (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/handle-card">>). `lares handle graft` stands as a stub over a built mint, where `publish`, `rotate`, `burn` and `attest` run live; the antigen's ban-`nym` move stays untouched; the browser's publish surface and a phone summons that presents the veil card stay owed. Flagged, unbuilt: a Handle's presenting cabal may also serve as its recovery cabal.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:544:* `X0` The founding bake: one deliberate re-genesis before a second operator stands, after which CIDs are meant to last because another operator pins them. It moves together `K15` step 6 (identity bytes, split stores, slot trees and FCKs, archive and custody formats, each face's random device veil), the place KEL's pre-rotation and the scoped place signer (the signer frames each duty's domain itself, signing `len(D) ‖ D ‖ preimage` and its verifiers the same, so no signed floor image carries its own separation; until then each of the five floor duties binds its domain by an exact head matcher), `W26`'s closing bake (the floor release), and `G37`'s preimage and format renames (`engine/v1` and its kin, the floor announcement's kind, the genesis seed and CAS formats). Each member carries its own readiness red, so the bake waits on the slowest by name, never on a date; the bake's own red: a fresh genesis founds, no CID from before the bake verifies after it, and a mixed old archive refuses by name. The gate it opens: a second operator may found a Nexus fresh at two of two. X.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:576:* `K14` The restored face's provisional standing (#/rulings; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/custody#/the-restore">>). The mark, guardian or chair view, confirm verbs and three authority-changing refusals stand. Owed: provisional guards at the root-signed crossing, edge kapae, device admit, two-founder act and session signer's authority purpose; a sibling view needs independent proof; the guardians' recovery path where every party stays unreachable. K, W, N.
