bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:286:* ''The floor vessel key drops its next-key commitment'', inside the one identity train. It changes the vessel's signed inception bytes; the operator may overturn it.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:335:* ''The vessel-identity family'': the persona roster, the worn-face selector, the pet-name map, the declaration map and the published-face record rest sealed under the S key as hot rows; each persona root rests as a cold row, opened for one act; the floor vessel key rests beside its signed inception, every load proves that inception, and no next-key seed or commitment rides it. The roster commits a root: a mint writes the root row, then the roster line that carries the root's public key, so a reading of a public key answers off the hot roster and opens no root. A root row with no roster line reads as an orphan: no reader holds it, `lares persona list` names it, and the same mint run again adopts it. A roster line whose root row went missing, or names another key, refuses by name at the act that needs the seed, and nothing mints over it. A hot row with nothing at its path reads as holding nothing; a row that stands and does not open, or opens to another shape, refuses by name at every read and every write. A vessel key mints only inside a held custody, and lands with its inception under the custody's one claim: the key file commits the mint, so two acts never commit two keys, and a boot loads a key and never mints one. The floor reads no row of the family, so a carried-Nexus reading by persona (a seated chair, a kept consent) answers empty until the key arrives, and a sovereign composition reads the roster whole before it stands (`packages/lararium-node/src/node-vessel-identity.ts`). A floor composition reads no roster, so it shuts every fleet lane: it sorts every device as set aside, sets a proven sibling aside, and its fetch door reads no peer as fleet, the pinned join gate's key included (`packages/lararium-node/src/floor-fleet-lanes.ts`). It still folds the one fleet board its own device edge names in the clear, so the Binding Gate reads this vessel's own seat at every standing.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:363:''R-CHARTER, the one AID train.'' Its first stage stands landed (train K of #/the-trains): the chairs sign with seat keys of their own and pre-rotate on cold cards, a Nexus answers to `nexus-<sha>`, the floor key commits no next key, per-Nexus keys mint at random, the PersonaGroup stands as a Keyhive group, and the Stable founding act founds a hearth (`lares vessel found --hearth`): the place, persona zero and a PRIVATE seed charter at one seat, with no keyring, every fleet relation bound to that charter's AID, and every harness that founds a hearth founding through it (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/founding-runbook#/found">>). What stays owed:
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:544:* `X0` The founding bake: one deliberate re-genesis before a second operator stands, after which CIDs are meant to last because another operator pins them. It moves together `K15` step 6 (identity bytes, split stores, slot trees and FCKs, archive and custody formats, each face's random device veil), the place KEL's pre-rotation and the scoped place signer (the signer frames each duty's domain itself, signing `len(D) ‖ D ‖ preimage` and its verifiers the same, so no signed floor image carries its own separation; until then each of the five floor duties binds its domain by an exact head matcher), `W26`'s closing bake (the floor release), and `G37`'s preimage and format renames (`engine/v1` and its kin, the floor announcement's kind, the genesis seed and CAS formats). Each member carries its own readiness red, so the bake waits on the slowest by name, never on a date; the bake's own red: a fresh genesis founds, no CID from before the bake verifies after it, and a mixed old archive refuses by name. The gate it opens: a second operator may found a Nexus fresh at two of two. X.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:696:# The rite's seam: `armGenesis` and `armRoll` hold every next-key line (inside `d209ce54b`).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:701:# The floor key commits no next key (`230907f66`).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:851:# ''House leans the operator may overturn'': the floor vessel key drops its next-key commitment; the long-silent device rule; the strangers' dial drops the newest arrival (#/decisions); the seal's standing leans (`S7` of #/the-loops).

